/*!
\page p_history History


RWMath actually traces its roots to two different math libraries.  They are EAMath, and an older RWMath library.  One
of the goals of the library was to create a unified library for legacy code that used EAMath, and legacy code that
used the older RWMath library.  The API that was created is essentially a union of the two API's with
a few changes.
-# Some function and types were modified for consistency or because they were misleading.
-# The library introduced a VecFloat type (and other associated types) for better performance on next-gen architectures.
-# Some functions were deprecated because of poor naming, or because they returned by reference.


*/
